From: ra80v2-nss project
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: widen the Q6/WCSS reserved region

ath11k hands the firmware raw physical addresses for the board data and the
m3 dump (qcom,bdf-addr / qcom,m3-dump-addr). On Xiaomi AX3000 (RA80v2) those
are 0x4c400000 for the built-in radio and 0x4d100000 / 0x4df00000 for the
QCN6122, but wcss@4b000000 only spans 0x4b000000-0x4cb00000, so the QCN6122
addresses are outside any reserved region and the built-in radio gets 7 MiB
where the firmware wants 13 MiB. Both radios then fail BDF download with
-ENOMEM:

    ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to load board data file: -12
    ath11k b00a040.wifi: failed to load board data file: -12

Expand wcss@4b000000 to 0x3000000 (48 MiB, 0x4b000000-0x4e000000) to fit both
radios in ath11k memory-mode 2 on 256 MiB RAM.

Signed-off-by: ra80v2-nss
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
 		};
 
 		q6_region: wcss@4b000000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x4b000000 0x0 0x1b00000>;
+			reg = <0x0 0x4b000000 0x0 0x3000000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
